    "keywords": "Initialize the store Migrate a workflow definition Recover from a format mismatch  Jobs and Workflows use database storage format 1. A workflow definitionversion is separate from that storage format. MigrateAsync changes aneligible workflow definition and does not change the database schema format. Run InitializeAsync during controlled deployment. Initialization serializesschema setup, checks the installed format and durable admission limits, andrejects an incompatible store. Start workers only after initializationsucceeds. Jobs persists payload and history limits. Workflows persists definition,input, result, signal, node, and history limits. You can adjust operationalbatch sizes, claim limits and command deadlines within the durableconfiguration. Rehearse changes on a restored backup before starting theupdated worker. Quiesce the instance before migrating. Any completed activity must keep itscompleted contract and result, and active work cannot be replaced. Pass theexpected instance revision so a stale update cannot overwrite new work.After migration, check that replay returns the same completed history andthat the new definition handles subsequent signals and timers. Keep a backup and a binary compatible with the written format. Avoid editingdatabase format markers to force a downgrade. For incompatible changes,restore a compatible backup or use the migration procedure supplied for thatformat. See upgrade Jobs for the worker rollout procedure."
